@packages/core/src/model/source.sigil import { SigilSourceModel }
@packages/core/src/model/diagnostics.sigil import { SigilDiagnosticModel }

component SigilRetrievalModel {
  goal {
    Define immutable purpose-retrieval targets, evidence, graphs, raw results, and
    agent-oriented projections.
  }

  interface {
    RetrievalModel {
      SigilSourceModel and SigilDiagnosticModel provide source and diagnostic data.

      *PurposeRetrievalResult* and its *target*, *graph*, *evidence*, *inclusion*,
      *exclusion*, *context*, and *fingerprint* data preserve deterministic
      retrieval output.
    }

    RetrievalProjection {
      RetrievalProjection is the separately versioned
      sigil-retrieval-projection/v1 agent presentation schema derived
      deterministically from one PurposeRetrievalResult.

      RetrievalProjection does not embed or re-export the raw
      sigil-purpose-retrieval/v1 result or its fingerprint. It leaves that
      result unchanged and derives a separate *projection fingerprint* from
      its own content.

      RetrievalProjection contains purpose, target, ordered *RetrievedComponent*
      entries, glossary entries derived from glossary-definition evidence in
      their existing order, diagnostics copied from the raw result in their
      existing order, and a projection fingerprint.

      A *projection glossary entry* has the canonical term and definition from
      one glossary-definition *EvidenceUnit*. It does not include occurrence
      records or unused *GlossaryFile* entries.

      RetrievedComponent has one stable *component identity*, path, one *role*,
      *component-owned links*, and one purpose-appropriate *contract projection*.
      When multiple graph relationships apply, its role uses the first
      applicable priority: *selected*, *dependency*, *importer*, then
      *cycle-member*. A *module-index summary* creates one module-context role
      only when no other RetrievedComponent already represents its exact
      component identity.

      A component-owned link has one *relation*, an exact target component
      identity, and its available import or *annotation location*. Links do
      not require a separate presentation-level relationship map.

      A selected component contract groups goal, interface, state, logic,
      constraints, decisions, and cases by their owning component.

      Every RetrievedComponent interface groups *SemanticUnits* by Concept when
      a *Tag identity* exists and retains ungrouped interface units without
      inventing a Concept.

      A non-selected dependency, importer, or cycle-member contract exposes
      only its goal and interface. A *module-context contract* exposes its
      selected summary sections only when that component identity has no
      other *projection entry*.

      Matching *expansion* SemanticUnits merge into the owning component and
      matching Concept or section. An expansion is not a presentation
      component, relationship category, or heading.

      *OwnershipLink* records an advisory implements, uses, or tests relation,
      a repository-relative one-way *implementation location*, optional symbol,
      and selected sections. It belongs to its owning component or Concept
      and does not prove implementation completeness or alignment.
    }
  }

  constraints {
    RetrievalProjection {
      Projection component identities and links are exact, stable, and resolvable
      within the same projection.

      A raw *graph edge* whose source or target does not correspond to a
      projected component is omitted from projection links. Every emitted
      link therefore resolves to an entry in the same projection.

      Projection ordering is deterministic. Components sort by selected status,
      *role priority*, *normalized path*, declaration start and end location with
      an absent location after a present location, component name, then
      *stable identity*. String comparisons use *Unicode scalar order* and
      numeric locations sort ascending. Links sort by relation, target identity,
      origin path, origin start and end location with an absent location after
      a present location, then stable source identity. Section units retain raw
      evidence order.

      Module-context components sort after cycle members and before no other
      component category; duplicate module-index summaries are omitted.

      Projection locations use normalized repository-relative paths and one-based
      line and column values already carried by raw retrieval evidence.

      A projection fingerprint covers purpose, target, components, glossary
      entries, and diagnostics in their emitted order, excluding the projection
      fingerprint field itself. It does not replace the raw
      PurposeRetrievalResult fingerprint.
    }
  }

  decisions {
    UnifiedRetrievalModel {
      Decision: Keep evidence-first retrieval and component-first projection in one
      SigilRetrievalModel while versioning their *wire contracts* separately.

      Scope: Governs semantic model ownership; excludes raw-result and
      projection consumer protocols.

      Rationale: Both contracts share *retrieval identities*, source locations,
      diagnostics, and deterministic derivation rules.

      Consequences: Consumers can evolve either schema independently while one
      semantic model governs their common invariants.
    }

    ProjectionRolePrecedence {
      Decision: Represent each RetrievedComponent with one highest-priority
      role: selected, dependency, importer, then cycle-member.

      Scope: Governs the agent-facing component role; excludes graph edges and
      component-owned links, which retain all selected relationships.

      Rationale: A single role keeps component grouping and ordering stable
      while the selected contract remains primary and each lower role conveys
      progressively less direct retrieval relevance.

      Consequences: Multiple raw relationships remain visible through links
      without duplicating a component or making its contract depend on evidence
      order.
    }

    ProjectionGlossary {
      Decision: Carry selected glossary-definition evidence on
      RetrievalProjection as ordered term-and-definition entries instead of
      making Markdown reread raw evidence.

      Scope: Governs agent-facing projection membership; excludes glossary
      selection, GlossaryFile authorship, and raw PurposeRetrievalResult shape.

      Rationale: RetrievalMarkdown takes the projection as its sole input,
      so omitted glossary entries cannot appear in Markdown without a second
      parse.

      Consequences: Projection fingerprints include glossary entries. Unused
      glossary rows remain absent.
    }

    AgentRetrievalProjection {
      Decision: Preserve the evidence-first PurposeRetrievalResult v1 protocol
      and derive a separately versioned component-first retrieval projection
      for agents.

      Scope: Governs agent-facing retrieval data and Markdown rendering;
      excludes raw retrieval membership, evidence, graph, ordering, JSON
      Lines, and compiler report protocols.

      Trade-offs: The projection adds a maintained schema, but avoids making
      every host reconstruct component, Concept, expansion, ownership, and
      link grouping.

      Design issues addressed: Flat evidence kinds expose expansions and source
      slices as peer content, producing repetitive Markdown that is difficult
      for people and agents to navigate.

      Discarded alternatives: Replacing raw v1 with a breaking grouped result
      and making every Markdown renderer infer groups from evidence were
      rejected.

      Consequences: Hosts can consume a stable grouped projection while
      automation retains the complete raw evidence result and its established
      fingerprint.

      Revisit when: A consumer requires a projection role, section, or relation
      that cannot be derived deterministically from purpose retrieval.
    }
  }

  cases {
    RetrievalProjection {
      A selected component with a MarkdownOutput Concept groups its declaration
      and matching expansion interface units beneath MarkdownOutput without an
      expansion heading.

      A selected component exposes its state, logic, constraints, decisions,
      and cases even when direct dependencies expose only their goal and
      interface.

      A component that is both a dependency and cycle member has dependency
      role; an importer that is also a cycle member has importer role.

      A graph edge whose endpoint has no projected component produces no
      component-owned link.

      An *ownership annotation* for a selected Concept becomes an
      OwnershipLink under that Concept with the annotation's repository-relative
      line and column.

      An implementation-purpose result contains advisory OwnershipLinks with
      a start location only and never embeds implementation-source slices.

      A dependency interface unit with a Tag identity occupies that named
      interface group on the dependency RetrievedComponent.

      Glossary-definition evidence becomes one projection glossary entry each
      and does not become a RetrievedComponent.
    }
  }
}
